    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm trying to refine our reorder logic for some lithium-ion battery cells we get from Shenzhen. We keep hitting stockouts during peak season because our lead times are pretty unpredictable. Can you help me draft a formula or some basic logic for calculating safety stock so we don't run dry while waiting for shipments?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A common approach to calculating safety stock is the \"verbal four-step method\" or the \"Triangular method.\" This involves calculating the mean, mode, and standard deviation of your historical lead times to estimate a reasonable safety stock level. The formula for safety stock is typically: Safety Stock = Standard Deviation x Desired Annual Tolerance for Inventory Outages x (1 - Desired Service Level).",
